      "content": "GREAT MISSENDEN        POTTER ROW SP 90 SW 2/92                                                 (west side) 22.12.58                                             Bury Farmhouse GV                                                      II Late C17, altered.  Red brick with some grey headers.  First floor band, gable walls rendered and painted and carried on to front wall as quoins.  Old tiled roof half hipped with large central brick stack with recessed panel and corbelled capping. Two modern hipped dormers and plaster coved cornice.  Two storeys, three modern casements central door replaced by window.  Modern rear wing in \"Tudor\" style. RCHM I p173 MON.5 Listing NGR: SP9061702100"
    }
